Z||000000||V8Fiero||03-23-2000||08:59 PM||||Hey all.<BR>On my 85 SE I need to replace the real wheel bearings. I have seen the whole hub assembly for sale and was wondering if its possible to just replace the bearings themselves instead of the whole thing? Havent had the chance or time to tear the rear end up to check. thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||03-23-2000||10:56 PM||||My father just had the right rear wheel bearings replaced on his 87, and they had to replace the whole hub.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||12:24 AM||||Well welcome to the forum, lets hear about this V8!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-24-2000||12:35 AM||||The rear wheel bearings are a sealed unit, not like the front ones.<P>The V8 clan is getting larger! I have a V8 85 SE too! Tell us more!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||03-24-2000||12:37 AM||||i believe all Fiero's used sealed hub/bearing assy. on the rear.  you need to buy the whole thing.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||03-24-2000||09:11 AM||||Replace both sides. The new hub units I got were signifigantly heavier construction than the stock ones. 84-87 all use the same hub unit.<P>You'll need a 30mm socket for the spindle nut and 18mm for the bolts.<P>In your case with a V8 I would replace the bolts and the spindle nut. ((You are suposed to replace the spindle nut every time it's removed. It is considered a lock nut and it degrades each time it is taken off.))<P>use a torque wrench to reinstall the bolts and nut. With the extra power of a V8 on them you want them all perfectly tightened.<P>When you are removing or replacing the spindle nut do it with the wheel on, the brakes locked, and the car one the ground. Use the spare tire if the regular wheels don't allow room or are to deep to work with. this will keep the suspension solid so you get an acurate reading on the torque wrench. It also makes it far easier to get the nut off. You will likely need a long bar or pipe to get it off.<P>DO NOT use an impact wrench on the spindle nut. You can damage the CV joints.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||04:48 PM||||ooops, I do everything you just said not to all the time.  I guess I need to stop huh?||||reg||1
Z||000007||V8Fiero||03-25-2000||02:29 AM||||Wow what a response. Great to be online. Well my V8 I have is pretty stock. 350 stock I mean. It goes pretty good. Beats the crap out of any V6 Fiero thats for sure. One point though. Make sure your starter is lined up correctly. Mine was but removed it to fix a oil leak and didnt put it back on correctly. Now I have to change the flywheel. Ate up some teeth on it. Have to beef up the suspension as well. Thanks again for all the responses. ||||reg||10
